 "notes": "Answers: ein is the business's EIN only, written in the EIN box; the SSN and ITIN boxes are never filled. One representative is asked for (rows 2 to 4 stay for the signer: the IRS sends notices to only two). Line 3 takes up to three rows: one matter, form and period per line (or ';') in the three answers. other_acts ticks the box and writes the text; 'None' leaves both blank, as does 'None' on deletions. A 'No' to a yes-or-no line leaves its single box blank. Part II (the representative's designation, licensing jurisdiction, bar or enrollment number, signature and date) belongs to the representative, and the taxpayer's signature and date to the signer. The XFA layer is dropped by the filler so the filled boxes show.",
